        content: `A very common and critical mistake made by first-time property buyers is assuming that executing the Sale Deed at the Sub-Registrar Office completes the ownership transfer. While a registered Sale Deed grants legal title between buyer and seller, you must complete Mutation (Dakhil Kharij) to update state government land revenue records.

Understanding the Mutation (Dakhil Kharij) Process:

• What is Dakhil Kharij? Dakhil Kharij is the formal revenue court process whereby the seller's name is removed (Kharij) from the official government Khatauni land register and replaced (Dakhil) with the buyer's name.
• Step-by-Step Procedure in UP:
  1. File Mutation Application: Submit a formal mutation application at the local Tehsil Revenue Court (or online via the UP Revenue Court Management System - RCMIS) within 30 days of registering the sale deed, attaching a certified copy of the registered Bainama.
  2. Public Notice Proclamation: The Revenue Court issues a mandatory 35-day public proclamation notice inviting any third-party objections.
  3. Final Revenue Order & Khatauni Entry: If no valid legal objections are received within the proclamation window, the Tehsildar or Naib Tehsildar passes the final Mutation Order.
  4. Obtain Updated Khatauni Copy: Download an updated copy of the Khatauni reflecting your name as the official recorded landowner. This updated Khatauni document is essential for future property resales, obtaining municipal water/electricity connections, securing bank home loans, and receiving government compensation in infrastructure expansion projects.`
